  <div id="sutta">
  
              <h2 id="SN1.18" class="h1">Shame<br/>
                Hiri Sutta  (SN 1:18)</h2>
              <p><em>This pair of verses provides an answer to the question posed and left unanswered in <a href="../KN/Dhp/Ch10.html#dhp143">Dhp 143</a>.</em></p>
              <div class="verse">
                <p>“Who in the world</p>
                <p>is a man constrained by shame,</p>
                <p>who awakens to censure</p>
                <p>like a fine stallion     to the whip?”</p>
                <div class="verse-add">
                  <p>“Those restrained by shame</p>
                  <p class="v3">are rare—</p>
                  <p>those who go through life</p>
                  <p class="v3">always mindful.</p>
                  <p>Having reached the end</p>
                  <p class="v1">of suffering &amp; stress,</p>
                  <p>they go among the discordant</p>
                  <p class="v3">harmoniously.”</p>
                </div>
              </div>
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
